WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Three million in Kiev could lose heat, water, and sanitation under Russia's winter strikes. This is Omni View, episode 238. After that, an Arab lawmaker takes a deputy speaker's chair in Israel, Ecuador's president denies a US base, and Nigeria approves a large security recruitment, then a global health warning, a second Lebanese airport, and a rural hospital that got its power back. Russia opened that bombing weeks earlier than anyone in these talks expected. The New York Times reported data

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.480
daily hits on the energy system, while American-led negotiations resumed last week in Abu Dhabi,

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.640
the capital of the United Arab Emirates, after nine months of quiet.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.980
In that room, Russia set out demands Ukraine and its European allies were unlikely to take.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.720
President Vladimir Zelensky said after a recent attack, they want to come to the table holding

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.080
our energy system hostage.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:57.140
The paper's reading of that hard line is that Moscow sees little reason to bargain now,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:02.020
because it thinks winter strikes will improve its position by spring. Nearly five

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:07.080
years in, the major war aims are still unmet, so infrastructure has become the strategy.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:12.780
Cities are more exposed than in earlier winters. The grid is already worn down, and air defenses

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:18.240
are running short. On Thursday, President Trump, President Vladimir Putin, and China's

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.260
Xi Jinping meet in Shen Zhen, and it is not clear they will talk about this war at all.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:28.828
A mod TB now holds a deputy speaker's chair in the Knesset, Israel's Parliament.

00:01:29.508 --> 00:01:32.588
Al Jazeera reported that fellow members elected him on Monday.

00:01:33.128 --> 00:01:37.988
He chairs the joint list, an alliance of parties representing Palestinian citizens of Israel,

00:01:38.608 --> 00:01:41.068
and he leads Taal, one party inside it.

00:01:41.528 --> 00:01:46.248
He called the post a rightful achievement for a list that won 11 seats on October 27.

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:52.208
Together with the United Arab List, known as Ram, those parties hold 19 seats in a house

00:01:52.208 --> 00:01:57.648
of 120, and they have endorsed Gadi Eisenkot to form the next government after President

00:01:57.648 --> 00:01:59.628
Isaac Herzog gave him that task.

00:02:00.288 --> 00:02:05.528
T.B. said Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's liquid party and National Security Minister

00:02:05.528 --> 00:02:08.868
Itamar Ben-Gveer tried to block his election and failed.

00:02:09.468 --> 00:02:11.328
He also wants a criminal investigation.

00:02:12.028 --> 00:02:16.948
Channel 12 reported that Netanyahu's chief of staff, Edo Norden, told police before

00:02:16.948 --> 00:02:21.908
the vote that three ROM activists in the South were carrying cash and vouchers to sway voters.

00:02:22.468 --> 00:02:27.008
Police used a former employee of the Prime Minister's office, then raided and arrested

00:02:27.008 --> 00:02:28.268
without valid warrants.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:32.088
TB wrote that no one is above the law, not even Netanyahu.

00:02:32.648 --> 00:02:38.288
He first won a seat in 1999 and was a deputy speaker from 2006 to 2022.

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:43.209
Ecuador's president says the American presence at Tower is not a base.

00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:49.069
Al Jazeera reported that Daniel Noboa denied it on Sunday, near the port of Guayaquil,

00:02:49.389 --> 00:02:53.509
after voters refused a referendum that would have allowed foreign military sites.

00:02:53.909 --> 00:03:00.069
The AFP news agency had already logged an unusual cluster of U.S. aircraft, dozens of tents,

00:03:00.369 --> 00:03:05.989
construction, about 20 military flights from June to mid-October, and papers that mentioned

00:03:05.989 --> 00:03:06.769
U.S. soldiers.

00:03:07.429 --> 00:03:10.189
Both the flights and the referendum result are on the record.

00:03:10.729 --> 00:03:11.789
What they mean is not.

00:03:11.789 --> 00:03:17.409
Noboa told the outlet Altavos the work is temporary, a mission, an operation,

00:03:17.749 --> 00:03:22.749
cooperation, and that the field remains Ecuadorian. His reason is the joint fight

00:03:22.749 --> 00:03:27.189
against drug trafficking. He did not speak to the aircraft count, and he stepped

00:03:27.189 --> 00:03:31.829
around a request to visit. Human Rights Watch calls that partnership perilous

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:36.649
because both governments have treated organized crime as a kind of war, and the

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:41.409
Watchdog says, committed serious human rights violations along the way. The

00:03:41.409 --> 00:03:45.269
The group is judging the partnership, not publishing its own headcount on the base.

00:03:45.929 --> 00:03:51.069
General Mauricio Salazar, then the Air Force commander, asked in a September letter whether

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:52.569
the deployment was even legal.

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:55.109
He was removed and sent to lesser duties.

00:03:55.809 --> 00:04:00.989
The Pentagon, Southern Command and Ecuador's Air Force had not answered AFP when that reporting

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:02.109
came out in October.

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:06.289
Watch whether Keto or Washington publishes the orders for those flights.

00:04:07.472 --> 00:04:10.872
Nigeria's president has signed off on a much larger security force.

00:04:10.872 --> 00:04:16.612
All Africa, citing Daily Trust, reported that the campaign counsel of the All Progressives

00:04:16.612 --> 00:04:23.812
Congress, Bola Tanubu's party, said he approved 28,000 more soldiers and 50,000 more police officers

00:04:23.812 --> 00:04:26.072
to take on insecurity nationwide.

00:04:26.672 --> 00:04:28.732
That is the counsel's account of an approval.

00:04:29.292 --> 00:04:31.912
It does not say when training or deployment would start.

00:04:32.864 --> 00:04:37.684
Drug-resistant infections could kill 39 million people over the next 25 years.

00:04:37.684 --> 00:04:43.264
the World Health Organization warned on Monday, and could turn ordinary surgery and childbirth

00:04:43.264 --> 00:04:49.984
dangerous. Al Jazeera reported the United Nations Health Agency's figures. In 2021, the resistance

00:04:49.984 --> 00:04:56.884
directly caused more than 1 million deaths and was linked to about 4.7 million more. In 2023,

00:04:57.284 --> 00:05:02.524
one in six lab confirmed bacterial infections reported to the agency shrugged off the antibiotic

00:05:02.524 --> 00:05:08.044
meant for it. Jean-Pierre Niemazi, Acting Head of that Department, said this threatens

00:05:08.044 --> 00:05:13.164
the future of modern medicine, and that unlike COVID-19, these deaths have piled up for

00:05:13.164 --> 00:05:19.624
years without the same alarm. Nearly 9 in 10 of 183 countries now have a national plan

00:05:20.124 --> 00:05:27.424
against about 4 in 10 in 2017. Pravasha Prakash, a technical officer, said only 42 countries

00:05:27.424 --> 00:05:31.824
fewer than one in five have a plan that is funded, running, and watched.

00:05:32.324 --> 00:05:37.544
Sylvia Bertagnolo, who leads surveillance, said that without a test, a doctor treats blind.

00:05:38.164 --> 00:05:42.964
The agency put out two tools, a list of tests that should exist from a local clinic up to

00:05:42.964 --> 00:05:48.384
a referral hospital, and a set of 73 lab steps from taking a sample to naming the germ

00:05:48.384 --> 00:05:54.784
and seeing which drug fails. Prevention, vaccines, clean water, and careful prescribing are the levers

00:05:54.784 --> 00:06:01.208
is it named. It also said the pace is still too slow for the 2030 targets. Lebanon is giving

00:06:01.208 --> 00:06:06.488
its second airport a date. Al-Jazeera reported that René Mouawad airport in the northern

00:06:06.488 --> 00:06:12.488
town of Clayat is set for test flights on Independence Day, November 22, and for commercial

00:06:12.488 --> 00:06:17.328
flights on December 14, when many Lebanese abroad come home for the winter holiday.

00:06:17.988 --> 00:06:23.028
Prime Minister Nawaf Salam flew a test from Beirut in June. The opening had been aimed

00:06:23.028 --> 00:06:27.788
at the middle of this year, then Israel's war delayed it, and construction pushed paying

00:06:27.788 --> 00:06:30.548
passengers from November 22nd into December.

00:06:31.108 --> 00:06:33.868
The split is over what a small northern runway is for.

00:06:34.388 --> 00:06:36.188
Officials say the point is economic.

00:06:36.808 --> 00:06:40.408
Air links for one of the poorest regions, time for holiday travel.

00:06:40.908 --> 00:06:46.128
Rafiq Hariri Airport, just south of Beirut, is still the only one in daily use, and

00:06:46.128 --> 00:06:51.728
in February 2025, supporters of Hezbollah, the Iranian-backed Shia-armed group, blocked

00:06:51.728 --> 00:06:55.368
the road into the capital when two Iranian planes were refused landing.

00:06:56.088 --> 00:07:00.848
Analyst Basel Duayk says that roadblock is a strategic advantage whenever the group and

00:07:00.848 --> 00:07:06.068
the government clash, and that Clayette only trims it because the new field is too small

00:07:06.068 --> 00:07:07.108
to replace Hariri.

00:07:07.828 --> 00:07:12.788
Analyst Marcel Balukji says the state still gains a fallback if Beirut's airport closes

00:07:12.788 --> 00:07:17.808
in a future war, especially for foreigners and diplomats, while conceding the new field

00:07:17.808 --> 00:07:19.548
does little about Hezbollah's weapons.

00:07:19.548 --> 00:07:23.488
Inflation is expected at 17.5% this year.

00:07:24.028 --> 00:07:28.308
The World Bank sees the economy shrinking 6.4% in 2026.

00:07:28.888 --> 00:07:32.188
Damage since 2023 has been put above $14 billion.

00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:38.988
The 2019 crash is still unrepaired under Israel's assault and the U.S.-Israel war on Iran.

00:07:39.943 --> 00:07:44.343
In Malawi, progress worth knowing is a rural hospital with the lights back on.

